What:           /sys/bus/i2c/devices/.../link_enable
Date:           September 2026
Description:
                LT7911EXC board link control (root writable). Write 1 to enable
                supplies, check chip communication, then connect CC. Write 0 to
                quiesce IRQ/work, isolate CC, then remove supplies. Read returns
                1 only after initialization succeeds; 0 means not ready/off.
                No video source is required for initialization to succeed.
                Active capture, firmware update or another transition returns
                EBUSY. Missing power/CC GPIOs returns EOPNOTSUPP. A userspace
                disable survives system suspend/resume, not a cold reboot.
                Runtime register access/stream start returns EHOSTDOWN while
                disabled. No GPIO reset pulse is issued on boards specifying
                lontium,no-reset-on-power-on; reset is released open drain.

What:           /sys/bus/i2c/devices/.../link_status
Date:           September 2026
Description:
                Read-only cached powered/ready/streaming/updating/suspended
                flags. Reading this snapshot never performs I2C transfers.
                Concurrent transitions may update the individual fields.

What:           /sys/bus/i2c/devices/.../registers
Date:           September 2026
Description:
                Read-only driver-serialized chip ID and video status snapshot.
                Does not access flash. Disabled link returns EHOSTDOWN; an
                exclusive operation already in progress returns EBUSY.
                Use this interface instead of forced i2c-dev register access.

What:           /sys/bus/i2c/devices/.../firmware_update
Date:           September 2026
Description:
                Existing root-only updater: write update or force. No automatic
                flashing is performed. Requires supplies on; rejects active
                capture. The power control lock is held throughout the update.
